      "standardized_narrative": "For Syndicate 510 in 2014, there was a net release of GBP 21.1 million in prior year reserves, primarily due to the reassessment of net claims incurred for previous accident years. This favorable development was noted across several lines of business, with claims settling for less than their reserves and benign claims development. However, there was also a general increase in reserves for the Cyber class and a conservative approach to reserving for the 2010 and 2011 New Zealand earthquakes.",
      "raw_causal_phrases": [
        "reduced reserves from prior years",
        "favourable claims development in many areas",
        "benign claims development during 2014, with the attritional incurred claims reducing over the year",
        "favourable claims development on prior years, including several cases where we have seen claims settling for less than their reserves",
        "reduced prior years reserves for a number of catastrophic events",
        "losses from the earthquakes that affected New Zealand in 2010 and 2011 still have significant reserves that have not yet been paid out to policyholders (and thus have not been paid by us to our reinsureds). As a consequence we are open to a greater degree of uncertainty than would be the case where losses are settled more rapidly, and we have thus taken a more conservative approach to the reserving of these events.",
        "favourable claims development and the release of certain outstanding claims",
        "older years settling out within our reserve projections",
        "GBP 0.3m strengthening of reserves on the prior years. This follows a new advice on the 2011 year of account, as well as a general increase in reserves on the Cyber class to align with market development data until it can be demonstrated that the book runs off faster than the benchmark.",
        "a surplus of GBP 21.1m (2013: GBP 32.9m) relates to the reassessment of net claims incurred for previous accident years."
